Back the MECHACON NVM S-commands with the user's own NVM: the host exposes a read-only
view, the OpenConfig area table and identity offsets of its MECHACON generation, and the
console model's MECHACON version (IopHost::mechaconNvm, PS2HostDevices::nvm). Serve the
version and console ID (0x03 sub 0x00/0x45), sceCdReadNVM (0x0A), sceCdRI (0x12), sceCdRM
(0x17) and sceCdOpenConfig/ReadConfig/CloseConfig (0x40/0x41/0x43) as PCSX2 CDVD.cpp does;
without an NVM they fail, and write sessions stay unsupported until NVM persistence exists.

